{"step_index":180,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-10-26T02:34:37Z","input_tokens":5086,"cache_read_tokens":30230,"output_tokens":6618,"thinking":"The user's preference for detailed, architect-grade documentation with rich visuals and precise references is noted. It's important to ensure the existing documentation, specifically the 16 ART wikis and the README, meet this standard. This will guide the effort to align the format and depth of information presented.\n\n\nInitial focus is on understanding the architecture of the Android Runtime (ART) through the provided wiki documents, particularly the layered execution engine and its compilation strategies. Expect to map the concepts of tiered compilation (Nterp, JIT, AOT) and their interplay with Class Hierarchy Analysis (CHA) and On-Stack Replacement (OSR). The goal is to establish a foundational understanding of ART's optimization pipeline.\n\nNext, investigating the Profile Guided Optimization (PGO) pipeline and its components. This encompasses profile collection, management tools, and the background optimization jobs. The aim is to clarify how PGO data influences the compilation process and contributes to runtime performance improvement.\n\nThen, delving into the mechanisms for accelerating application startup, specifically class and image preloading techniques. Key interest lies in how `BootImage`, `JitZygote`, `AppImage`, and `RuntimeImage` contribute to reducing application initialization time. The role of `madvise` and startup tasks in memory management will also be examined.\n\nFinally, the focus will shift to JNI optimization. The plan is to decipher how to achieve high-performance JNI transitions, specifically the identified optimization strategies. The expectation is to identify the crucial elements that enable efficient inter-language method calls.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"invoke_subagent","args":{"Prompt":"\"请执行 **Task 01**，深入研读 `/home/ethen/workspace/voya